pervisors\nFor current PhD students\nPhD induction\nMRes Experimental Neuroscience\nMSc Translational Neuroscience\nBSc Neuroscience and Mental Health\nMeet our students\nMeet our teaching staff\nInformation for current MRes and MSc students\nUndergraduate Research Opportunities Programme (UROP)\nStudent experience\nWork Experience Programme for Year 12\nResearch\nNeurology\nCerebral small vessel disease (cSVD)\nNeuroscience\nPsychiatry\nAddiction research\nChild and adolescent mental health research\nCOVID-19 and Mental Health\nLEAP2 study\nMood Instability Research\nNCORE: Neural Correlates of Reward and Emotion in opioid dependence\nSPS study\nPhD opportunities\nNews and events\nOutreach\nNewsletter and blog\nCommunications and media\nHealth and safety\nContact us\nBrain Sciences news\nBrain Sciences events\nFor staff\nEvents calendar (Outlook)\nKey contacts\nHR forms, resources and training\nTraining requirements for staff involved in recruitment\nMental health and wellbeing resources\nPhysical and Mental Health First Aiders\nMentoring\nRegister your public engagement activities\nFor parents and carers\nLGBTQ+ Allies network\nReward and Recognition scheme\nAwards\nEquality, diversity and inclusion\nCommunications and media\nBrand assets\nIn this section\nDepartment of Brain Sciences\nApplication FAQs\nHow to apply\nFunding\nInformation for supervisors\nFor current PhD students\nDepartment of Brain Sciences\nImperial Home\nFaculty of Medicine\nDepartments\nDepartment of Brain Sciences\nStudy\nPhD opportunities\nPhD opportunities\nStudy\nApplication FAQs\nHow to apply\nFunding\nInformation for supervisors\nFor current PhD students\nPlay video\nBrian Schilder shares insights into his journey as a PhD student based in the Department of Brain Sciences\nThe Department of Brain Sciences provides an ideal environment to pursue a PhD and build your career in research. As a postgraduate research student, you'll have access to state-of-the-art facilities and work alongside our world-leading academic staff in a dynamic and supportive research environment. We welcome applications from outstanding students from around the world, provided they meet the College's eligibility criteria.\nBelow, you'll find further information about how to apply and the latest funding opportunities available within the Department. Guidance is also available for current supervisors and PhD students.\nEvery year, the Faculty hosts Rising Scientist Day, a networking event for all PhD, MPhil and MD (Res) students.\nPhD links\nHow to apply\nGuidance on how to apply a PhD or MD (Res) within the Department.\nLearn more\nFunding\nBrowse PhD funding opportunities in the Department.\nLearn more\nInformation for supervisors\nExplore guidance and eligibility information for research degree supervisors.\nLearn more\nInformation for current PhD students\nPolicies, processes and further support for current PhD students in the Department.\nLearn more\nDr Miriam Ries\n\"After my PhD in Brain Sciences, I went on to do a postdoc at ETH Zurich. I have now moved to the area of research management, first as scientific coordinator of several multi-centre research projects, and now managing projects and initiatives within one professorship. During my PhD, I enjoyed the freedom within my research and the supervision of students, but also my engagement outside of my project, as student representative and in outreach programmes. I encourage all PhD students to remain open to and aware of the many career paths for which a PhD can be the first stepping stone. I also wish I\u2019d taken advantage of more of Imperial\u2019s offers, such as the swimming pool!\"\nApplication FAQs\nGeneral PhD enquiries\nFor all PhD-related enquiries, please contact us via email at researchdegreeenquiries@imperial.ac.uk\nResearch Degrees Administrator (Records)\nCasper Debieux\nResearch Degrees Administrator (Admissions)\nCallum Gray\nResearch Degrees Manager\nHayley Kendall-Berry\nDirector of Postgraduate Research\nProfessor Kevin Murphy\nContact and Links\nDepartment of Brain Sciences\nAddress\nBurlington Danes Building,\nThe Hammersmith Hospital Campus,\nDu Cane Road,\nLondon W12 0NN\nHammersmith Campus map\nFind us on social media\nX, formerly known as Twitter\nLinkedIn\nBlueSky\nUseful Links\nPopular links\nCanvas\nContact the Service Desk\nJobs\nLibrary services\nOutlook email online\nFaculties\nEngineering\nMedicine\nNatural Sciences\nImperial Business School\nDirectories\nAdmin and support services\nNetworks and Centres\nResearch groups\nSearch all staff\nPartners\nImperial College Academic Health Science Centre\nImperial College Health Partners\nImperial College Healthcare NHS Trust\nImperial Consultants\nCollege Information\nImperial College London\nAddress\nImperial College London\nSouth Kensington Campus\nLondon\nSW7 2AZ, UK\ntel: +44 (0)20 7589 5111\nFacebook\nX, formerly known as Twitter\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nTikTok\nBluesky\nSite Information\nSitemap\nAccessibility\nModern slavery statement\nPrivacy notice\nUse of cookies\nReport incorrect content\nLog in\n\u00a9 2026 Imperial College London", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/brain-sciences/study/phd-opportunities/#content"], ["View accessibility support page", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about-the-site/accessibility/"], ["", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/"], ["Study", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/study/"], ["Research", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/research-and-innovation/"], ["Faculties", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/faculties-and-departments/"], ["News", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/news/"], ["Events", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/whats-on/"], ["About", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about/"], ["Get involved", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/get-involved/"], ["Giving", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/giving/"], ["Shop Imperial", "https://shopimperial.org/"], ["Search", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/search"], ["", "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/"], ["Skip to section navigation", "https:/